    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d861">

                <pb facs="0934" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg648"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 341.622a/144</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Austro-Hungarian Chargé</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Zwiedinek</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1567</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 31, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 11</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to your valued note No.
                        241<anchor n="1" xml:id="d861-f1"/> of the 19th of this month and in
                    continuation of my note No. 1521<anchor n="1" xml:id="d861-f2"/> of May 24
                    relative to the Austrian and Hungarian subjects taken from the S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">China</hi>, I have the honor to inform your excellency
                    that according to a report of the Imperial and Royal Legation at Peking that has
                    now reached the Embassy, Isidor H. Gieras (?), Ferdinand Würth, and Paul Zednik
                    are not liable to military service. Alexander Camerle. Karl Breckner, Alfred
                    Schiefler, Anton Gerl, and Anton Piety, do belong to the military organization
                    but, according to their passports, are merchants.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Zwiedinek</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
